### Compare shortcut keys in display order

**Severity:** `medium`

`HashSet.SetEquals` treats two lists as equal even when their order differs. `Keys` is a display list, so an order change can be suppressed and leave the visual shortcut stale.

Compare each element at the same index after the count check and return false on the first mismatch.

```suggestion
            for (int index = 0; index < currentValue.Count; index++)
            {
                if (!Equals(currentValue[index], newValue[index]))
                {
                    return false;
                }
            }

            return true;
```

**Verification:** Exercise shortcuts whose modifier/code list changes order and confirm the visual list refreshes only when ordered values differ.
